{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When a quarter's demand (contract reservation) exceeds what is produced and available from inventory, is the shortfall allowed to be carried over as backorder into the next quarter (incurring the delay compensation), or must every quarter's demand be fully satisfied within that same quarter?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding how to handle unmet demand (backlog vs. immediate satisfaction), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the delay compensation, if a unit of product I is produced in quarter 2 but its contract was for quarter 1, is the cost 20 yuan (one quarter late), and if it is delivered in quarter 3, is the cost 40 yuan (two quarters late) — i.e., does the penalty accumulate per quarter of delay for each unit?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the calculation method for delay penalties, using specific examples to confirm if the cost accumulates linearly per quarter."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The 15,000 production hours per quarter limit — does it apply to the total hours used to produce all three products combined in that quarter (i.e., 2×units of I + 4×units of II + 3×units of III ≤ 15,000), or is it a separate limit for each product?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the scope of the production hour limit (combined vs. per product)."
}

